      "id": 16210,
      "name": "WarrenAC",
      "username": "WarrenAC",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/d2c977/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-02-20T17:59:41.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I was doing a Vengeance matchup - Prime Wardens Fanatic, &nbsp;Bunker (Engine of War) and Dark Watch Mr. Fixer fighting Proletariat, Friction and Ermine - and came across an interesting interaction I hadn't seen before. &nbsp;I was using Prime Warden Fanatic's power - you take damage, &nbsp;play a card, &nbsp;and anyone can use a power - and she pulled Prayer of Desperation out. &nbsp;I know normally when you play it on your turn it ends things right away, &nbsp;but this was the powers phase and I was allowed to still trigger a power use. &nbsp;Not sure if this was intentional or there's something about doing this not in your card play phase that treat turns a bit differently (maybe your turn is already over, or the power use triggers retroactively because the Power was used before the card took effect?) I guess it's a bit of \"how immediately is immediately\".</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:51.228Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
