    {
      "id": 190302,
      "name": "grysqrl",
      "username": "grysqrl",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/{size}/1909_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-02-20T21:12:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>To be clear, \"end your turn\" means \"go to your end-of-turn phase\"; so your turn isn't done, but you may skip one or more of your previous phases.</p><p>\"skip the rest of your turn\", however stops everything and immediately goes to the next turn. You see this on Meteor Storm, for example.</p>",
